Z||000003||Fierowrecker||09-08-2001||01:22 AM||||Hey Cruzer!<BR>Is it an auto or manual?<BR>If it is an auto, change the filter and fluid...<BR>DO NOT GET IT FLUSHED!!!<BR>I have heard of it wrecking the tranny, and the wife's van has had 3 trannys, and she USED to get it flushed...<BR>I have had the same problem with my auto trans Fiero...<BR>crash...<P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||09-08-2001||01:42 AM||||Starting to think all those 'rumors' about fiero's might be true after all?  Mine hasn't gone up in a blaze yet, but it sure has a lot of problems that my pocketbook can't handle all at once.....so it tries to be nice by getting a new problem once I have fixed and paid for a previous problem.  I think it's just testing my nerves.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Galen||09-08-2001||02:38 AM||||Is a 80's vette any more reliable? a 80's chevette? Citation?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||8Ball||09-08-2001||02:44 AM||||No offense to anyone but.....<P><BR>I hear alot of people talking bad about their Fiero's (and I get frustrated too sometimes) when something breaks of needs fixed or what not. BUT it is an older car in need of work. How many problems do you think the owners of 57's have??? I know. LOTS. So just because the car has some problems don't fall into the path of thinking that a Fiero is a bad car. It just needs love. And if your stomping of the gas and raceing your 15 or so year old engine then you should expect no less. (Side note, I am guilty of doing it once or twice myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<BR>Anyway, never lose faith in the Fiero is all I am trying to say.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||09-08-2001||04:35 AM||||You couldn't of said it any better 8Ball. There are a lot of things you have to consider when your Fiero starts giving you problems:<P>a) Even my 88GT has it's share of problems. There are at least 10 small things that it needs.<P>b) My GT is 13 years old and has 100K miles on it. The only cars that have that many miles and are still somewhat reliable are Jap.<P>c) This car is eccentric and UNIQUE. American technology has never caught up with Japanese. They build it better because they have too. If they didn't we would see no reason to export their stuff.<P>d) The only tried and true way to keep your Fiero reliable is to have it all fixed at one time, cover it in the garage, and never drive it anywhere but to get detailed. Did I mention that that would negate the reason for having one in the first place?<P>They are great cars, but they do need TLC.<BR>What made me get another one? The sensations and feelings I had behind the wheel of my first, a red/silver 86 SE V6 with all the goodies and a 4 speed.<P>I sold a great NEW motorcycle for the $ to get my GT because it gives me many of the same pleasures with A/C, stereo, and a SEATBELT.<BR>I'll pay to have someone yank the motor and rebuild it if and when (knock on wood) it comes to that because they truly are different,eccentric, and very very unique for an american.<P>Sly<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000008||artherd||09-08-2001||05:07 AM||||Take a number...<P><BR>Any car's reliability is directly proportional to how it is cared for by it's owners.<P>Some people treat their cars like poop, and expect them to go 1,000,000miles withought flaw.<P>I choose to look at it another way, my LIFE depends on this hunk of metal, so I'm going to treat it right.   I drive in a fassion mid-engine sports cars were created for, but I *take care* of the car too.<P>I look for stuff that is about to break, and fix it with stuff that won't.  <P>Engines pontiac put in suck? I put in better stuff.    A little bit (or a lot, the Fiero is 'a lot' of car to me.) of both preventative and *pro-active* matinence will keep your car on the road, and in as-new or better safety, as long as you own it.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
