Z||000018||Haagster||09-08-2001||10:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 8Ball:<BR><B>I hear alot of people talking bad about their Fiero's (and I get frustrated too sometimes) when something breaks of needs fixed or what not. BUT it is an older car in need of work. How many problems do you think the owners of 57's have??? I know. LOTS. So just because the car has some problems don't fall into the path of thinking that a Fiero is a bad car. It just needs love. And if your stomping of the gas and raceing your 15 or so year old engine then you should expect no less. (Side note, I am guilty of doing it once or twice myself   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<BR>Anyway, never lose faith in the Fiero is all I am trying to say.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I gripe about my Fiero, but truth be known I knew when I bought the car what I was getting into with it.  I went through all of the "repair and replace" with my coupe when I bought it in 96, and am now going through the same thing with the GT.  It is not that it is a bad car (or POS), I just like to hear myself complain about it.<P>BTW:  I plan to have it all fixed for my son's 16th birthday (he is 4 years old).<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
